========================================================================
MANUAL STEPS: three platform datasets are not publicly downloadable
========================================================================
Each needs vendor registration and is large. Stage them by hand:

Vizgen MERSCOPE mouse brain -> /media/steve/USB/github/workshop2026aug_data/spatial_imaging/vizgen_mouse_brain/s2r1/
  Register at https://info.vizgen.com/mouse-brain-data and download
  slice 2 replicate 1. LoadVizgen expects the MERSCOPE output files
  (cell_by_gene.csv, cell_metadata.csv, detected_transcripts.csv, ...).

Nanostring CosMx lung (raw) -> /media/steve/USB/github/workshop2026aug_data/spatial_imaging/nanostring_lung5_rep1/
  From https://nanostring.com/products/cosmx-spatial-molecular-imager/ffpe-dataset/
  Lung5 Rep1. The precomputed annotations are already staged, so this
  raw directory is only needed to run LoadNanostring live.

Akoya CODEX lymph node -> /media/steve/USB/github/workshop2026aug_data/spatial_imaging/akoya_lymph_node/
  LN7910_20_008_11022020_reg001_compensated.csv, from the HuBMAP portal
  via Globus.

If you will not obtain these, present only the Xenium and CosMx
sections, which are fully staged. The .qmd sections for the missing
platforms will error at their Load* call, which is expected.
========================================================================

Done. spatial_imaging (public parts staged; manual steps above if any)

========================================================================
